decision_conditions:
Condition : 7 - The illuminated advertisement hereby approved shall comply with the following terms:
(a) Between the hours of sunset and sunrise, the intensity of the illumination of the advertisement shall not exceed 300 cd/m2 as recommended by the Institution of Lighting Professionals (ILP, PLG05) or maximum limits as permitted by any guidance that supersedes this;
(b) Between the hours of sunrise and sunset, either no lighting, or the  maximum lighting levels (such as for digital displays) are set in accord with nighttime maximums, or controlled so they comply with the guidance approach to ambient lighting as recommended by the Institution of Lighting Professionals (ILP, PLG05) or maximum limits as permitted by any guidance that supersedes this;
(c) The minimum display time for each advertisement shall be 10 seconds, the use of message sequencing for the same product is prohibited and the advertisements shall not include features/equipment which would allow interactive messages/advertisements to be displayed.        
(d) There shall be no special effects (including noise, smell, smoke, animation, exposed cold cathode tubing, flashing, scrolling, three dimensional, intermittent or video elements) of any kind during the time that any message is displayed. This is in the interest of highway safety.    
Reason: In the interests of amenity and highway safety.
